# blutspender cron schedule
#
# Install with:
#   crontab deploy/crontab
# Verify with:
#   crontab -l
#
# Installing REPLACES your whole user crontab — it does not append. Check what is
# there first with "crontab -l".
#
# The clone path is hardcoded in the "cd" of every job below. If you cloned
# somewhere other than /srv/blutspender, change all three.
# Times are local; set the VPS clock with: timedatectl set-timezone Europe/Berlin

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# Parse DRK appointments for the day `offset` days out (config.json), then drop
# everything with date <= today. Runtime scales with the number of result pages —
# usually a few minutes.
#
# Late evening on purpose, and it MUST finish before midnight. The parser ends by
# calling delete_outdated_data(), which deletes date <= today using the clock at
# that moment — so a run that spilled past 00:00 would delete the new current day
# instead of the old one. With offset=8 the parser only ever fetches the single
# day 8 days out, so a day deleted that way is never re-fetched: it would just be
# missing. 23:00 leaves an hour of headroom; do not move this closer to midnight.
0 23 * * * cd /srv/blutspender && ./deploy/run-job.sh parser

# Notify users about appointments near them. Reads the window the parser left
# behind last night, today included.
30 7 * * * cd /srv/blutspender && ./deploy/run-job.sh sender

# Nightly database dump, rotated locally and pushed offsite if RCLONE_REMOTE is set.
0 3 * * * cd /srv/blutspender && ./deploy/run-job.sh backup

# Reclaim space from old images/layers after rebuilds. Volumes are untouched.
0 4 * * 0 docker image prune -af --filter "until=168h" > /dev/null 2>&1
